middle-schoolers

639
00:25:18,050 --> 00:25:19,785
to play clarinet with
them 'til the wee hours,

640
00:25:19,818 --> 00:25:22,322
waking them the next day to
whisper in their tender ears,

641
00:25:22,355 --> 00:25:23,790
I say more power to him!

642
00:25:23,823 --> 00:25:25,725
Mr. Servo, you're
evading the question!

643
00:25:25,758 --> 00:25:28,462
If, by this sir, you mean
that Mr. B Natural is a man,

644
00:25:28,495 --> 00:25:29,762
I challenge you to
come up with any

645
00:25:29,795 --> 00:25:31,698
condemning evidence
to the contrary.

646
00:25:31,732 --> 00:25:33,500
They named him mister
and I, for one,

647
00:25:33,533 --> 00:25:35,135
have faith that they knew
what they were doing.

648
00:25:35,168 --> 00:25:36,603
You might as well just ask me

649
00:25:36,637 --> 00:25:38,037
to prove that a fish is a fish.

650
00:25:38,070 --> 00:25:39,672
Gentlemen, it just is.

651
00:25:39,705 --> 00:25:42,775
As for these phantom breasts
Mr. Robot claims to have seen,

652
00:25:42,808 --> 00:25:44,978
I say, phooey-kaflooey.

653
00:25:45,012 --> 00:25:46,747
Perhaps he's been
in space too long.

654
00:25:46,780 --> 00:25:49,148
Gentlemen, Mr. B
Natural is just that.

655
00:25:49,182 --> 00:25:51,952
Here's wishing we could all
be a little bit more like him.

656
00:25:51,985 --> 00:25:53,118
I yield the floor.

657
00:25:53,152 --> 00:25:54,955
Mr. T. Robot, you
have 20 minutes to rebut.

658
00:25:54,988 --> 00:25:57,757
Mr. Servo, you have
got to be kidding me!

659
00:25:57,790 --> 00:26:00,293
Let's assume, for the moment,
that Mr. B Natural is a man.

660
00:26:00,327 --> 00:26:03,630
My heavens, what a confusing
message to send to little kids.

661
00:26:03,663 --> 00:26:05,865
Already, there's the painful
feeling of isolation,

662
00:26:05,898 --> 00:26:07,733
the horrible scarring acne,

663
00:26:07,767 --> 00:26:10,670
and Mr. Servo, here, would
have us place a cross-dressing

664
00:26:10,703 --> 00:26:13,407
man with a clarinet
slap-dab in their bedrooms.

665
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:15,642
Why not men in Little
Bo Peep costumes

666
00:26:15,675 --> 00:26:17,377
with stinky cigars,
explaining the facts of life

667
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:18,712
to our unsuspecting daughters?

668
00:26:18,745 --> 00:26:21,213
- I, for one, would not--
- Mr. Servo, your rebuttal!

669
00:26:21,247 --> 00:26:22,848
Yes, yes, why not, Mr. Crow?

670
00:26:22,882 --> 00:26:24,217
I don't think we
should stop there.

671
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:25,552
Let's break down
all the barriers.

672
00:26:25,585 --> 00:26:27,687
Hairy men in spartan
costumes holding bake sales

673
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:30,523
on shady boulevards,
naked jockstrap wrestling

674
00:26:30,557 --> 00:26:31,725
big, wonderful--

675
00:26:31,758 --> 00:26:33,627
Gentlemen, I have
commercial sign, I'm sorry.

676
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:38,298
(new wave music)

677
00:26:39,932 --> 00:26:41,300
Okay, I don't want
anymore fighting.

678
00:26:41,333 --> 00:26:42,435
Look, Crow,
remove the breasts

679
00:26:42,468 --> 00:26:43,403
and your whole
argument falls apart.

680
00:26:43,437 --> 00:26:45,372
Colossal breast, see?

681
00:26:45,405 --> 00:26:46,940
Beast. Beast!

682
00:26:46,973 --> 00:26:48,342
To prove how
tough this Ford is,

683
00:26:48,375 --> 00:26:52,312
we're pitting it against
the amazing, Colossal Beast.

684
00:26:52,345 --> 00:26:55,182
Breast, beast.

685
00:26:55,215 --> 00:26:56,415
Becwar?

686
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:58,618
Yes, Becwar, the
William Shatner novel.

687
00:26:58,652 --> 00:27:02,988
- (laughs) It's TekWar.
- Oh, never mind.

688
00:27:03,022 --> 00:27:04,823
Cute joke though.

689
00:27:04,857 --> 00:27:08,060
(all gasp)
We're watching okay?

690
00:27:08,093 --> 00:27:11,798
There's got Albert
Glasser here, the music.

691
00:27:13,633 --> 00:27:14,700
It's peppy.

692
00:27:14,733 --> 00:27:16,268
In a turgid sort of way.

693
00:27:16,302 --> 00:27:19,238
Hey, it's Ralph Macchio
as the Colossal Kid.

694
00:27:19,272 --> 00:27:21,473
I love Ralph Macchio.

695
00:27:21,507 --> 00:27:22,675
(all gasp)

696
00:27:22,708 --> 00:27:24,943
And he's being
chased by credits.

697
00:27:26,478 --> 00:27:27,380
(applause and cheers)

698
00:27:27,413 --> 00:27:28,147
Yay! But what's the I stand for?

699
00:27:28,180 --> 00:27:29,782
I am so ashamed.

700
00:27:29,815 --> 00:27:32,885
Music composed and
conducted by Albert Glasser.

701
00:27:32,918 --> 00:27:34,787
A Domino guy and
