1891
01:13:45,522 --> 01:13:47,523
All mild. All one.

1892
01:13:47,557 --> 01:13:50,693
Dilute for baby bath,
beach, body, shampoo,

1893
01:13:50,727 --> 01:13:52,997
sauna, and Chinese
essene burial ritual.

1894
01:13:53,030 --> 01:13:57,533
Dilute. Dilute. OK. All
One. Miracle of universe.

1895
01:13:57,567 --> 01:13:59,637
Impossible below PH3.

1896
01:13:59,670 --> 01:14:03,207
Absolute clean: Apply
Vaseline, oil, butter or cream.

1897
01:14:03,240 --> 01:14:05,408
Insert teaspoon
juicy lemon pulp.

1898
01:14:05,442 --> 01:14:07,577
Gotta go.

1899
01:14:07,610 --> 01:14:08,878
Has anybody seen him?

1900
01:14:08,912 --> 01:14:11,782
No. Tally Ho.

1901
01:14:11,815 --> 01:14:12,248
(barking)

1902
01:14:12,282 --> 01:14:16,553
(new wave music)

1903
01:14:19,557 --> 01:14:21,090
I was just actin'
screwy you guys.

1904
01:14:21,123 --> 01:14:22,392
I'll say.

1905
01:14:22,425 --> 01:14:23,393
I was just clownin' around.

1906
01:14:23,427 --> 01:14:25,662
Any opinion yet,
Dr. Richardson?

1907
01:14:25,695 --> 01:14:29,365
We're not ready to
publish yet. But he's big.

1908
01:14:29,398 --> 01:14:30,633
His parents
said he fell down.

1909
01:14:30,667 --> 01:14:32,135
He must have hit
his head on the rocks.

1910
01:14:32,168 --> 01:14:33,470
Of course the
wounds went untended,

1911
01:14:33,503 --> 01:14:37,607
so scar tissue
formed as you see it.

1912
01:14:37,640 --> 01:14:38,675
The shock of
such a fall would

1913
01:14:38,708 --> 01:14:40,410
indicate the
possibility of amnesia.

1914
01:14:40,443 --> 01:14:43,280
Milk of amnesia.

1915
01:14:43,313 --> 01:14:44,748
I don't understand it.

1916
01:14:44,782 --> 01:14:46,583
I get a normal,
nervous reaction,

1917
01:14:46,617 --> 01:14:49,352
that's certainly not
typical of amnesia.

1918
01:14:49,385 --> 01:14:51,455
Get a load of Mr.
Stage Business over there.

1919
01:14:51,488 --> 01:14:52,588
What's he doin'?

1920
01:14:52,622 --> 01:14:55,258
Are you ready for
the association tests?

1921
01:14:55,292 --> 01:14:56,427
You ready, Phil?

1922
01:14:56,460 --> 01:14:58,895
Oh, I'm in this
movie. I forgot.

1923
01:15:00,730 --> 01:15:04,333
Part one: toilet training.

1924
01:15:04,367 --> 01:15:09,673
Golden Books presents,
the World of Geography.

1925
01:15:09,707 --> 01:15:13,877
Glenn Manning. Look at
the picture in front of you.

1926
01:15:13,910 --> 01:15:15,112
I dare ya.

1927
01:15:15,145 --> 01:15:16,647
Does it mean anything to you?

1928
01:15:16,680 --> 01:15:18,615
It's your tax
dollars at work, Glenn.

1929
01:15:18,648 --> 01:15:20,783
You went to college
there, Manning.

1930
01:15:20,817 --> 01:15:22,852
(grunting)

1931
01:15:22,887 --> 01:15:25,688
We're gonna try another.
We're not getting any response.

1932
01:15:25,722 --> 01:15:27,390
Glenn, this is the Lusitania.

1933
01:15:27,423 --> 01:15:28,558
It has nothing to
do with your life,

1934
01:15:28,592 --> 01:15:30,360
but it was in the
packet in the gift shop.

1935
01:15:30,393 --> 01:15:32,062
Look again, Manning.

1936
01:15:32,095 --> 01:15:33,363
Look at this ship.

1937
01:15:33,397 --> 01:15:34,530
Your mother was on that ship.

1938
01:15:34,565 --> 01:15:35,598
It brought you back
to this country

1939
01:15:35,632 --> 01:15:37,033
after your service in Korea.

1940
01:15:37,067 --> 01:15:39,803
Your mother! Mother!

1941
01:15:41,170 --> 01:15:43,240
Does this bug you Glenn?

1942
01:15:43,273 --> 01:15:44,642
Try another one.

1943
01:15:44,675 --> 01:15:45,708
Glenn!

1944
01:15:45,742 --> 01:15:47,410
This is Sy Sperling,
President of Hair Club.

1945
01:15:47,443 --> 01:15:50,447
Look at this face.

1946
01:15:50,480 --> 01:15:51,682
Do you recognize it?

1947
01:15:51,715 --> 01:15:53,183
It's supposed to be you.

1948
01:15:53,217 --> 01:15:54,652
(grunting)

1949
01:15:54,685 --> 01:15:55,785
Won't spend much time on
this one, next slide please.

1950
01:15:55,818 --> 01:15:58,488
Does this man
mean anything to you?

1951
01:16:00,490 --> 01:16:01,358
You have five seconds.

1952
01:16:01,392 --> 01:16:03,560
Do you understand?

1953
01:16:03,593 --> 01:16:04,828
It's your face!

1954
01:16:04,862 --> 01:16:06,697
We'll come back to
this one if we have time,

1955
01:16:06,730 --> 01:16:08,598
but they're gonna
get harder now.

1956
01:16:08,632 --> 01:16:10,233
What do you think Doc?

1957
01:16:10,267 --> 01:16:11,402
I like the picture
of his college.

1958
01:16:11,435 --> 01:16:12,302
I don't see a
use in continuing.

1959
01:16:12,335 --> 01:16:14,103
He doesn't seem to respond.

1960
01:16:14,137 --> 01:16:16,105
Let me try, please.

1961
01:16:17,207 --> 01:16:18,442
Remember these.

1962
01:16:18,475 --> 01:16:21,645
You must
remember, Glenn, try.

1963
01:16:21,678 --> 01:16:25,582
Your childhood. Remember
your bicycle, Glenn?

1964
01:16:25,615 --> 01:16:27,750
It was red and it
had a light on it.

1965
01:16:27,783 --> 01:16:29,552
And you hit me with it.

1966
01:16:29,585 --> 01:16:31,655
We had fun when we were
kids, didn't we Glenn?

1967
01:16:31,688 --> 01:16:35,092
We had joy, we had fun, we
had seasons in the sun, Glenn.

1968
01:16:35,125 --> 01:16:37,160
Your first high school date.

1969
01:16:37,193 --> 01:16:41,130
When Dad let you take the
car. You were so proud.

1970
01:16:41,163 --> 01:16:42,598
Now you're an
enfeebled freak.

1971
01:16:42,632 --> 01:16:44,467
You must remember, Glenn.

1972
01:16:44,500 --> 01:16:45,735
You must remember this.

1973
01:16:45,768 --> 01:16:46,870
A kiss is still a kiss.

1974
01:16:46,903 --> 01:16:49,640
Please, Glenn.
Please try to remember.

1975
01:16:49,673 --> 01:16:52,775
(grunting loudly)

1976
01:16:54,377 --> 01:16:56,012
Glenn.

1977
01:16:56,747 --> 01:16:58,415
Oh my goodness, he's flashing

1978
01:16:58,448 --> 01:17:01,452
on the Uncle Dan in
the closet thing.

1979
01:17:01,485 --> 01:17:02,618
Glenn.

1980
01:17:02,652 --> 01:17:03,887
(screaming loudly)

1981
01:17:03,920 --> 01:17:07,790
You were a big help.
The slides were working.

1982
01:17:12,662 --> 01:17:17,100
I got nowhere else
to go. I got nothin'.

1983
01:17:17,133 --> 01:17:20,637
Giant fails last chance.
Giant fails last chance.

1984
01:17:20,670 --> 01:17:24,207
What does that mean?
He's gonna get the chair?

1985
01:17:24,240 --> 01:17:27,110
Now, how are they gonna
make a chair that big?

1986
01:17:27,143 --> 01:17:29,078
Have any money on him?

1987
01:17:30,280 --> 01:17:31,815
Get your orders?

1988
01:17:31,848 --> 01:17:34,685
Shipping him out
tomorrow morning.

1989
01:17:34,718 --> 01:17:37,687
The Navy has a ship ready
to take him to the island.

1990
01:17:37,720 --> 01:17:40,657
It's a small one about
60 miles off the coast.

1991
01:17:40,690 --> 01:17:43,060
Nice beach, good view.

1992
01:17:43,093 --> 01:17:44,962
It'll take all
night to get him ready.

1993
01:17:44,995 --> 01:17:47,930
Sponge bath alone will
take two, three hours.

1994
01:17:47,963 --> 01:17:48,998
Told Joyce yet?

1995
01:17:49,032 --> 01:17:50,733
No.

1996
01:17:50,767 --> 01:17:54,570
You better.
She's at her hotel.

1997
01:17:54,603 --> 01:17:57,640
I'll see you back here
in about a half an hour.

1998
01:17:57,673 --> 01:18:00,677
Thanks for the cheek marks
on the desk, Eisenhower.

1999
01:18:00,710 --> 01:18:03,847
(door closes)

2000
01:18:03,880 --> 01:18:06,650
Nah, I still don't get Zippy.

2001
01:18:08,718 --> 01:18:13,157
(suspenseful classical music)

2002
01:18:13,190 --> 01:18:16,358
Sounds kind of like Lurch.

2003
01:18:16,393 --> 01:18:17,660
He's all blocked up.

2004
01:18:17,693 --> 01:18:19,797
Think he's got an itch.

2005
01:18:19,830 --> 01:18:21,163
Love in the time of colitis.

2006
01:18:21,197 --> 01:18:22,165
He'll be well provided for.

2007
01:18:22,198 --> 01:18:23,633
An airlift is being
setup and food will

2008
01:18:23,667 --> 01:18:25,068
be parachuted down to him.

2009
01:18:25,102 --> 01:18:26,437
And he has a trust fund.

2010
01:18:26,470 --> 01:18:27,403
He'll be supplied
with everything he needs.

2011
01:18:27,437 --> 01:18:28,605
Is that a clock?

2012
01:18:28,638 --> 01:18:30,340
Just the same, it's horrible.

2013
01:18:30,373 --> 01:18:31,575
No, that's an astro-light.

2014
01:18:31,608 --> 01:18:32,508
There's no place
in the civilized

2015
01:18:32,542 --> 01:18:33,810
world for a creature that big.

2016
01:18:33,843 --> 01:18:34,945
So, we're sending
him to Cleveland.

2017
01:18:34,978 --> 01:18:36,278
Have you seen
what's happened to him?

2018
01:18:36,312 --> 01:18:37,580
He'll be happier by himself.

2019
01:18:37,613 --> 01:18:39,048
I haven't got time for this.

2020
01:18:39,082 --> 01:18:40,317
I suppose I should
agree with you,

2021
01:18:40,350 --> 01:18:44,755
but I can't help feeling
terribly sorry for him.

2022
01:18:44,788 --> 01:18:46,557
Well, look at it
this way, Glenn has

2023
01:18:46,590 --> 01:18:48,225
become a total stranger to you.

2024
01:18:48,258 --> 01:18:50,593
He's not your brother
anymore, but a monster.

2025
01:18:50,627 --> 01:18:52,662
With the instincts
of a wild beast.

2026
01:18:52,695 --> 01:18:54,563
But that happens
in families...

2027
01:18:54,597 --> 01:18:55,832
There's nothing you and
I, or anyone else can do

2028
01:18:55,865 --> 01:18:58,968
that will ever change him
back to what he once was.

2029
01:19:00,270 --> 01:19:02,005
Anchors away, Glenn (laughs).

2030
01:19:02,038 --> 01:19:03,707
I love teasing him like that.

2031
01:19:03,740 --> 01:19:05,775
Private, don't
tease the giant.

2032
01:19:05,808 --> 01:19:08,112
(suspenseful music)

2033
01:19:10,547 --> 01:19:15,018
Oh heck, stay together
cheeks. Excuse me.

2034
01:19:19,722 --> 01:19:23,760
(snoring jokingly)

2035
01:19:23,793 --> 01:19:26,663
It's kind of like the
great escape of Glenn's head.

2036
01:19:26,697 --> 01:19:29,867
(spooky classical music)

2037
01:19:40,810 --> 01:19:44,680
This is bull. I'm
outta here. This bites.

2038
01:19:44,713 --> 01:19:46,683
Will he be alone
on this island?

2039
01:19:46,717 --> 01:19:47,917
The Navy will
land an inspection.

2040
01:19:47,950 --> 01:19:48,918
What is this, 20 questions?

2041
01:19:48,952 --> 01:19:50,087
He's goin' to an
island. Come on.

2042
01:19:50,120 --> 01:19:51,722
I'd like to go
with him, if I can.

2043
01:19:51,755 --> 01:19:53,690
I thought you would. So
it's been arranged for you.

2044
01:19:53,723 --> 01:19:54,992
Goodnight Joyce.

2045
01:19:55,025 --> 01:19:55,592
Oh, wait.

2046
01:19:55,625 --> 01:19:56,793
Really?

2047
01:19:56,827 --> 01:19:57,727
I know you've done
everything you can

2048
01:19:57,760 --> 01:20:00,497
for him Mark, and for me.

2049
01:20:00,530 --> 01:20:01,598
Thank you.

2050
01:20:01,632 --> 01:20:03,267
Is that a big jack
with lights on it?

2051
01:20:03,300 --> 01:20:05,535
(phone rings)

2052
01:20:05,568 --> 01:20:07,003
It's just a lamp.

2053
01:20:07,037 --> 01:20:08,172
Hello?

2054
01:20:08,205 --> 01:20:10,340
Major Baird? Just a
moment, he's right here.

2055
01:20:10,373 --> 01:20:12,508
Hee-haw, it's Sam Wainwright.

2056
01:20:12,542 --> 01:20:14,510
Major Baird here.

2057
01:20:14,543 --> 01:20:16,378
(dramatic dark music)
When?

2058
01:20:16,412 --> 01:20:19,215
Well, he was checked
OK just 10 minutes ago.

2059
01:20:19,248 --> 01:20:20,517
Glenn has escaped.

2060
01:20:20,550 --> 01:20:21,952
He snuck out.

2061
01:20:21,985 --> 01:20:23,720
Let me speak
to Dr. Carmichael.

2062
01:20:23,753 --> 01:20:25,222
I can't sir, he's dead.

2063
01:20:25,255 --> 01:20:27,657
Therefore, unable
to come to the phone.

2064
01:20:27,690 --> 01:20:29,692
Round up the
usual large suspects.

2065
01:20:29,725 --> 01:20:31,293
This is an
all-points bulletin.

2066
01:20:31,327 --> 01:20:33,763
The Colossal Man is
loose in Los Angeles.

2067
01:20:33,797 --> 01:20:36,432
All units report
immediately upon contact.

2068
01:20:36,465 --> 01:20:40,270
I repeat: The Colossal Man
is loose in Los Angeles.

2069
01:20:40,303 --> 01:20:42,538
All units report
immediately upon contact.

2070
01:20:42,572 --> 01:20:44,140
Pep Boys and Dinettes.

2071
01:20:44,173 --> 01:20:45,408
(sirens wailing)

2072
01:20:45,442 --> 01:20:48,378
There's a giant on the loose
and he's got a big caboose.

2073
01:20:48,412 --> 01:20:50,713
Car 54, where are you?

2074
01:20:50,747 --> 01:20:53,417
Meanwhile, at
the Daily Planet...

2075
01:20:56,787 --> 01:20:57,820
Will they know where you are?

2076
01:20:57,853 --> 01:20:58,955
Hope not, wanna drink?

2077
01:20:58,988 --> 01:21:00,190
Yes, I told Harris we'll be

2078
01:21:00,223 --> 01:21:02,025
here in the office
waiting for news.

2079
01:21:02,058 --> 01:21:05,295
I've got a silk kimono,
mind if I slip into it?

2080
01:21:05,328 --> 01:21:06,830
Let me have the
police department.

2081
01:21:06,863 --> 01:21:08,665
I have't even
tried anything yet.

2082
01:21:08,698 --> 01:21:10,733
I'm calling for Major Baird.

2083
01:21:10,767 --> 01:21:12,002
Grrr.

2084
01:21:12,035 --> 01:21:14,203
Yes, we know he's escaped.
Has he been sighted yet?

2085
01:21:14,237 --> 01:21:16,372
Who is he, Mr.
Rogers all of a sudden?

2086
01:21:16,405 --> 01:21:17,707
I see.

2087
01:21:17,740 --> 01:21:19,775
Like the sporty
look? Is this OK?

2088
01:21:19,808 --> 01:21:23,713
No police reports,
he hasn't been seen.

2089
01:21:23,747 --> 01:21:25,648
Where could he be?

2090
01:21:25,682 --> 01:21:27,650
He signed with the
William Morris Agency,

2091
01:21:27,683 --> 01:21:30,153
now we'll never find him.

2092
01:21:31,755 --> 01:21:33,623
Quo Vadis, with
Peter Ustinov.

2093
01:21:33,657 --> 01:21:35,825
(phone rings)

2094
01:21:35,858 --> 01:21:38,662
Hello, shadow-y office? Grrr.

2095
01:21:38,695 --> 01:21:40,697
He's been spotted
in Griffith Park.

2096
01:21:40,730 --> 01:21:42,165
Do you have a map?

2097
01:21:42,198 --> 01:21:43,833
Yes, I've got the map of
Griffith Park right here.

2098
01:21:43,867 --> 01:21:46,737
I'm the same guy
in the same office.

2099
01:21:46,770 --> 01:21:47,970
Surround the
area and move the

2100
01:21:48,003 --> 01:21:49,438
infantry in on him
'til we make contact.

2101
01:21:49,472 --> 01:21:50,573
Yes sir.

2102
01:21:50,607 --> 01:21:52,242
Don't open fire 'til he's
isolated from all civilians.

2103
01:21:52,275 --> 01:21:53,310
Yes sir.

2104
01:21:53,343 --> 01:21:54,477
And then only if
absolutely necessary.

2105
01:21:54,510 --> 01:21:55,645
Yes sir.

2106
01:21:55,678 --> 01:21:57,247
Have the place block
off all access roads.

2107
01:21:57,280 --> 01:21:58,482
- Yes sir.
- They're good at that.

2108
01:21:58,515 --> 01:21:59,648
Move up our communications.

2109
01:21:59,682 --> 01:22:01,217
We'll setup the
headquarters in the hills.

2110
01:22:01,250 --> 01:22:01,885
Yes sir.

2111
01:22:01,918 --> 01:22:03,653
I'll take command.

2112
01:22:03,687 --> 01:22:06,322
Right.

2113
01:22:06,923 --> 01:22:08,658
I declare Martial law.

2114
01:22:08,692 --> 01:22:11,327
Attention all units.
Attention all units.

2115
01:22:11,360 --> 01:22:14,163
The Colossal Man is in
the Griffith Park area.

2116
01:22:14,197 --> 01:22:18,435
Get the description right.
Male, Caucasian. 60 feet tall.

2117
01:22:18,468 --> 01:22:22,738
Answers to the name
Glenn or Hey Big Guy.

2118
01:22:22,772 --> 01:22:24,807
Proceed to the
Ferndale entrance.

2119
01:22:24,840 --> 01:22:28,077
Road blocks will
be setup at once.

2120
01:22:28,110 --> 01:22:29,212
We interrupt our
regular program to

2121
01:22:29,245 --> 01:22:31,247
bring you a special
police bulletin.

2122
01:22:31,280 --> 01:22:33,583
The Colossal Man
has broken loose.

2123
01:22:33,617 --> 01:22:37,020
And is now known to be in the
vicinity of Griffith Park.

2124
01:22:37,053 --> 01:22:38,722
Steps are being taken
to recapture him.

2125
01:22:38,755 --> 01:22:39,888
It's Jack Lemmon.

2126
01:22:39,922 --> 01:22:41,892
Do not go near
the area. I repeat.

2127
01:22:41,925 --> 01:22:44,427
Do not go near the area.

2128
01:22:44,460 --> 01:22:45,695
You may endanger your
life by doing so.

2129
01:22:45,728 --> 01:22:46,763
Hey, let's go near the area.

2130
01:22:46,797 --> 01:22:48,063
You are certain
to impede emergency

2131
01:22:48,097 --> 01:22:51,167
services which need all
the space they can get.

2132
01:22:51,200 --> 01:22:53,168
This station is dispatching
a mobile unit for

2133
01:22:53,202 --> 01:22:56,205
on the spot coverage at
the scene in Griffith Park.

2134
01:22:56,238 --> 01:22:59,308
Ktla, over and out.
Keep watching the skies.

2135
01:22:59,342 --> 01:23:00,610
Oh, I see.

2136
01:23:00,643 --> 01:23:04,313
They let the bus from Duluth
go near the area, but we can't.

2137
01:23:04,347 --> 01:23:07,517
It's the cast of
Rebel Without a Cause.

2138
01:23:07,550 --> 01:23:08,885
They get to go near the area.

2139
01:23:08,918 --> 01:23:11,420
(people chattering)

2140
01:23:12,822 --> 01:23:16,727
Car 54, where are you?

2141
01:23:16,760 --> 01:23:18,462
One Adam 12. See the man.

2142
01:23:18,495 --> 01:23:21,363
Neighbors report giant man
kicking over garbage cans.

2143
01:23:21,397 --> 01:23:23,032
Hey bud, pull out.

2144
01:23:23,065 --> 01:23:24,500
I'm waiting for
a load of kids.

2145
01:23:24,533 --> 01:23:25,235
Where are they?

2146
01:23:25,268 --> 01:23:26,737
In the Griffith Observatory,

2147
01:23:26,770 --> 01:23:27,970
lookin' for a
sputnik or something.

2148
01:23:28,003 --> 01:23:29,038
Hurry them up and get out of

2149
01:23:29,072 --> 01:23:30,373
the park as quick as you can.

2150
01:23:30,407 --> 01:23:31,473
What's gonna happen?

2151
01:23:31,507 --> 01:23:33,943
There's trouble. The giant
man is loose around here.

2152
01:23:33,977 --> 01:23:35,445
What, are these
kids in night-school?

2153
01:23:35,478 --> 01:23:38,882
No. Day for night-school.
It's Hollywood.

2154
01:23:38,915 --> 01:23:40,917
Let's go. Hurry
it up. All aboard.

2155
01:23:40,950 --> 01:23:42,852
Come on, I got a bus to move.

2156
01:23:42,885 --> 01:23:45,188
Ha. Bust-a-move.

2157
01:23:46,990 --> 01:23:51,527
(new wave music)

2158
01:23:52,562 --> 01:23:54,863
Can I have a gun? You
said I could have a gun.

2159
01:23:54,897 --> 01:23:56,632
Setup a road block here.

2160
01:23:56,665 --> 01:23:58,602
He's somewhere between
us and the observatory.

2161
01:23:58,635 --> 01:23:59,502
A road block?

2162
01:23:59,535 --> 01:24:00,703
Why don't you just draw a line

2163
01:24:00,737 --> 01:24:03,105
on the highway and tell
him not to cross it?

2164
01:24:03,105 --> 01:24:04,440
Give me my boom box.

2165
01:24:04,507 --> 01:24:07,010
(suspenseful music)

2166
01:24:09,612 --> 01:24:12,948
Yep. A lot of films
crashed on this curve.

2167
01:24:18,455 --> 01:24:20,823
Check it out. It's
the Tonight Show's set.

2168
01:24:20,823 --> 01:24:22,525
I didn't know that.

2169
01:24:22,558 --> 01:24:23,727
So that's what they're doin'.

2170
01:24:23,760 --> 01:24:26,162
Jeez, we're really
up here aren't we?

2171
01:24:29,865 --> 01:24:31,233
We're gonna go with
our Haggar slacks now?

2172
01:24:31,267 --> 01:24:32,268
Hmm-mmm.

2173
01:24:32,335 --> 01:24:33,537
Nice.

2174
01:24:33,570 --> 01:24:36,472
This is Major Baird at
the Griffith Park road block.

2175
01:24:36,538 --> 01:24:38,575
You're not gonna believe
where I'm calling you from.

2176
01:24:38,642 --> 01:24:41,243
I'm outside, on a shoe phone.

2177
01:24:42,845 --> 01:24:44,847
Oh, it's a premier.

2178
01:24:44,847 --> 01:24:48,885
They're gonna send
out Army Archer next.

2179
01:24:48,952 --> 01:24:51,988
It's a used car
sell-a-thon. What a feeling.

2180
01:24:55,392 --> 01:24:57,660
Ladies and gentlemen,
you're witnessing a manhunt--

2181
01:24:57,693 --> 01:24:58,862
Ktla is everywhere.

2182
01:24:58,895 --> 01:25:01,163
For the biggest
man in existence.

2183
01:25:01,197 --> 01:25:05,902
We're in Griffith Park. It's
been surrounded by troops.

2184
01:25:05,968 --> 01:25:07,070
Big troops.

2185
01:25:07,103 --> 01:25:10,807
They're moving out
to try to make contact.

2186
01:25:10,873 --> 01:25:12,742
We're hoping he breaks into
song when we lights at him.

2187
01:25:12,775 --> 01:25:13,710
That building
your seeing there

2188
01:25:13,743 --> 01:25:16,312
is the Griffith Observatory.

2189
01:25:16,345 --> 01:25:20,283
It's a nice place. You
should visit sometime.

2190
01:25:20,317 --> 01:25:23,085
The giant is tearing
people apart like bread.

2191
01:25:23,118 --> 01:25:26,322
No, I just added that.
Journalistic license, and all.

2192
01:25:26,355 --> 01:25:28,758
Anyway, back to Rebel
Without a Cause.

2193
01:25:28,792 --> 01:25:30,793
Remember, this is brought to you

2194
01:25:30,827 --> 01:25:33,797
by True Value Hardware stores.

2195
01:25:33,830 --> 01:25:36,598
Put your clothes
on, it's the cops.

2196
01:25:37,700 --> 01:25:39,635
I want a jury to cover
the mountain on all sides.

2197
01:25:39,668 --> 01:25:40,837
A jury? What kinda jury?

2198
01:25:40,870 --> 01:25:43,005
Particularly here and here.

2199
01:25:46,108 --> 01:25:48,678
Funny-face tank.

2200
01:25:48,712 --> 01:25:50,580
Cuddly funny tank.

2201
01:25:51,647 --> 01:25:54,183
This is the tanks I get.

2202
01:25:54,850 --> 01:25:57,653
That was a real Jeep joke.

2203
01:25:57,687 --> 01:26:01,257
Get the Bat Signal ready.

2204
01:26:01,290 --> 01:26:03,325
Flashlight tag. You're it.

2205
01:26:04,560 --> 01:26:09,465
Wait, I'm not ready. Two,
three, four. How does it start?

2206
01:26:09,498 --> 01:26:10,800
He's parked on an
incline, you're gonna

2207
01:26:10,833 --> 01:26:14,037
want to turn those
wheels probably.

2208
01:26:14,070 --> 01:26:17,673
Rat patrol, pass it on.
Rat patrol, pass it on.

2209
01:26:20,210 --> 01:26:24,447
Arthur? Laurie?
Hurry, we're leaving now.

2210
01:26:24,480 --> 01:26:27,517
Sure, I'd go up in a rocket
ship. What's to stop me?

2211
01:26:27,550 --> 01:26:29,285
They've got all of
the problems solved.

2212
01:26:29,318 --> 01:26:31,153
You wouldn't have
anybody to talk to.

2213
01:26:31,187 --> 01:26:32,622
This kid has a rocket
in his pocket I think.

2214
01:26:32,655 --> 01:26:34,723
I'm cold. I wish Mom
would've made me bring my coat.

2215
01:26:34,757 --> 01:26:36,025
Girls mature faster.

2216
01:26:36,058 --> 01:26:37,660
I'd talk to all the people
back on earth by radio.

2217
01:26:37,693 --> 01:26:39,728
Maybe I'd even call you, Laurie.

2218
01:26:39,762 --> 01:26:40,730
Laurie.

2219
01:26:40,763 --> 01:26:41,863
That way, when your
father's objecting to you

2220
01:26:41,898 --> 01:26:43,365
talking on the phone too long,

2221
01:26:43,398 --> 01:26:45,368
you just tell him it
was someone on the moon.

2222
01:26:45,402 --> 01:26:47,203
That wouldn't make any
difference to my father.

2223
01:26:47,237 --> 01:26:48,872
What, are we suddenly
in a different movie?

2224
01:26:48,905 --> 01:26:50,773
What's going on?

2225
01:26:50,807 --> 01:26:52,475
Maybe the
martians have landed.

2226
01:26:52,508 --> 01:26:54,477
The teacher's
been calling us.

2227
01:26:54,510 --> 01:26:55,512
Let her call.

2228
01:26:55,545 --> 01:26:57,847
Boy, look at all
those search lights.

2229
01:26:57,880 --> 01:26:59,115
Ktla knows you.

2230
01:26:59,148 --> 01:27:01,483
We're going to meet
some of the officers.

2231
01:27:01,517 --> 01:27:03,218
We couldn't have
done it without him.

2232
01:27:03,252 --> 01:27:04,587
Any trouble with the public

2233
01:27:04,620 --> 01:27:07,123
causing congestion
in the disaster area?

2234
01:27:07,157 --> 01:27:08,290
Not this time.

2235
01:27:08,323 --> 01:27:09,258
They seem to be
keeping the roads

2236
01:27:09,292 --> 01:27:10,360
pretty well open for us.

2237
01:27:10,393 --> 01:27:11,560
Sounds like the
cop's kinda congested.

2238
01:27:11,593 --> 01:27:13,128
I understand you were
able to get everyone out

2239
01:27:13,162 --> 01:27:13,797
of the park before anything
could happen to them.

2240
01:27:13,830 --> 01:27:15,298
That's right.

2241
01:27:15,332 --> 01:27:17,267
We really appreciate you
men at a time like this.

2242
01:27:17,300 --> 01:27:19,335
Quit kissing up, Ktla.

2243
01:27:19,368 --> 01:27:21,703
Oh, there's Glenn now. That's
the top of the observatory.

2244
01:27:21,737 --> 01:27:25,140
(people murmuring)

2245
01:27:25,173 --> 01:27:27,610
Oh officer, there was
a tour bus from Westmont

2246
01:27:27,643 --> 01:27:29,845
Junior High up at the
planetarium tonight.

2247
01:27:29,878 --> 01:27:31,280
Did you see it come down?

2248
01:27:31,313 --> 01:27:33,750
All cars were checked out
of the park sometime ago.

2249
01:27:33,783 --> 01:27:34,783
Are you sure?

2250
01:27:34,817 --> 01:27:36,152
My daughter Laurie was on it.

2251
01:27:36,185 --> 01:27:38,220
I've been waiting for
her down at the corner.

2252
01:27:38,253 --> 01:27:39,622
You see, we live in Glendale.

2253
01:27:39,655 --> 01:27:41,357
And I thought if I
picked her up here

2254
01:27:41,390 --> 01:27:42,525
and drove her home, she
could get her sleep.

2255
01:27:42,558 --> 01:27:43,793
Yeah, yeah. Make
it short, sister.

2256
01:27:43,827 --> 01:27:45,027
I got things to do.

2257
01:27:45,060 --> 01:27:46,195
She has to get up so
early on school days.

2258
01:27:46,228 --> 01:27:48,363
I brought her coat
in case she's cold.

2259
01:27:48,397 --> 01:27:49,665
Wait a minute and I'll check.

2260
01:27:49,698 --> 01:27:51,500
Thank you.

2261
01:27:51,533 --> 01:27:53,937
- Arthur? Laurie?
- We better go.

2262
01:27:53,970 --> 01:27:56,772
Cut it out mom,
I'm makin' time.

2263
01:27:58,507 --> 01:28:00,242
There's nothing for
you to worry about.

2264
01:28:00,275 --> 01:28:02,545
The bus is still up there
but it seems to be safe.

2265
01:28:02,578 --> 01:28:05,315
Can't I go through? Let
me go to Laurie, please.

2266
01:28:05,348 --> 01:28:06,548
She ought to have her coat.

2267
01:28:06,582 --> 01:28:08,383
I wanted her to take it
when she left the house.

2268
01:28:08,417 --> 01:28:10,887
Yeah, you told
me that already.

2269
01:28:10,920 --> 01:28:12,555
She'll be all
right without it.

2270
01:28:12,588 --> 01:28:14,457
Just you take it easy
and wait right here.

2271
01:28:14,490 --> 01:28:16,592
Lost in the valley of
the shadow of the sub-plot.

2272
01:28:16,625 --> 01:28:18,895
Laurie Edwardson, Arthur
Lang, where have you been?

2273
01:28:18,928 --> 01:28:20,028
Coming of age?

2274
01:28:20,062 --> 01:28:21,530
Over there,
watchin' the lights.

2275
01:28:21,563 --> 01:28:23,098
They're a lot of
people down there.

2276
01:28:23,132 --> 01:28:24,367
Something's the matter.

2277
01:28:24,400 --> 01:28:26,035
Well get in the bus,
quickly. We have to go.

2278
01:28:26,068 --> 01:28:28,303
Look, look at the giant!

2279
01:28:28,337 --> 01:28:30,540
Oh yeah, hi. How are ya?
I get that all the time.

2280
01:28:30,573 --> 01:28:33,743
Seen it. I'm a
lineman for the county.

2281
01:28:36,045 --> 01:28:37,713
Ktla, no.

2282
01:28:37,747 --> 01:28:38,815
He's tremendous.

2283
01:28:38,848 --> 01:28:40,450
(people exclaiming)

2284
01:28:40,483 --> 01:28:43,753
Wait, I think I see Humphrey
Bogart in Emot Ett Kvitto.

2285
01:28:43,787 --> 01:28:48,323
(mysterious music)

2286
01:28:52,295 --> 01:28:54,163
A Spielberg film
all of a sudden.

2287
01:28:54,197 --> 01:28:56,565
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for being here.

2288
01:28:56,598 --> 01:28:58,300
I didn't know it was
gonna be stand up only.

2289
01:28:58,333 --> 01:29:00,737
I used to live in a circus tent.

2290
01:29:02,572 --> 01:29:05,340
Glenn Manning.
You are surrounded.

2291
01:29:05,375 --> 01:29:06,508
By people who love you.

2292
01:29:06,542 --> 01:29:08,110
It is impossible
for you to escape.

2293
01:29:08,143 --> 01:29:10,580
We wanna show
you more slides.

2294
01:29:11,780 --> 01:29:14,083
(grunting)

2295
01:29:14,117 --> 01:29:15,117
Is that Ktla down there?

2296
01:29:15,150 --> 01:29:16,685
I wanna talk straight to Ktla.

2297
01:29:16,718 --> 01:29:18,855
(grunting)

2298
01:29:18,888 --> 01:29:22,558
I repeat. Escape
is impossible.

2299
01:29:22,592 --> 01:29:25,795
You won't be harmed if you
give yourself up at once.

2300
01:29:25,828 --> 01:29:28,463
I've heard that before.

2301
01:29:30,198 --> 01:29:31,633
Give yourself up, Glenn.

2302
01:29:31,667 --> 01:29:32,702
To a higher power.

2303
01:29:32,735 --> 01:29:34,670
Give yourself up.

2304
01:29:34,703 --> 01:29:37,107
Surrender yourself or
you will be destroyed.

2305
01:29:37,140 --> 01:29:38,908
I'll see they go easy on ya.

2306
01:29:38,942 --> 01:29:41,477
(ominous music)

2307
01:29:43,612 --> 01:29:45,380
(grunting)

2308
01:29:45,415 --> 01:29:48,818
Come on cop-per, you'll
never take me alive.

2309
01:29:50,018 --> 01:29:52,488
Grr. Grr.

2310
01:29:52,522 --> 01:29:55,792
Spotlight dance,
Glenn Manning.

2311
01:29:58,962 --> 01:30:01,797
(screams loudly)

2312
01:30:01,830 --> 01:30:02,565
(children screaming)

2313
01:30:02,598 --> 01:30:04,033
Oh Willy, I
can see the house.

2314
01:30:04,067 --> 01:30:07,970
That's Laurie's bus. Please
let me go. That's Laurie.

2315
01:30:08,003 --> 01:30:11,207
Don't you think somebody's
got to do something?

2316
01:30:11,240 --> 01:30:13,575
I've seen bigger
guys than that before.

2317
01:30:14,910 --> 01:30:17,813
This is a job for Superman.

2318
01:30:17,847 --> 01:30:19,915
(sobbing)

2319
01:30:21,183 --> 01:30:23,987
(mumbling)
Hey, stop, wait, come back.

2320
01:30:24,020 --> 01:30:25,655
Joyce, come back.

2321
01:30:25,688 --> 01:30:27,757
You still have to
write Fennegan's Wake.

2322
01:30:27,790 --> 01:30:30,860
(ominous music)

2323
01:30:30,893 --> 01:30:32,328
Hey, hold the bus.

2324
01:30:32,362 --> 01:30:35,330
(children screaming)

2325
01:30:44,440 --> 01:30:46,975
- Laurie!
- Stella!

2326
01:30:47,008 --> 01:30:48,912
McCloud!

2327
01:30:48,945 --> 01:30:51,913
(crying) Laurie.

2328
01:30:57,653 --> 01:31:01,190
Glenn W. Manning, you come
right down here this instant.

2329
01:31:01,223 --> 01:31:02,925
Put that down right now.

2330
01:31:02,958 --> 01:31:04,193
Put it down.

2331
01:31:04,227 --> 01:31:06,328
I'm the God, I'm the God!

2332
01:31:06,362 --> 01:31:08,063
Listen to me Glenn, please.

2333
01:31:08,097 --> 01:31:09,032
I'd call this a good argument

2334
01:31:09,065 --> 01:31:10,465
against bussing, wouldn't you?

2335
01:31:10,500 --> 01:31:11,400
What if you bus
your kids, they

2336
01:31:11,433 --> 01:31:13,202
might get picked up by a giant?

2337
01:31:13,235 --> 01:31:14,103
You never know.

2338
01:31:14,137 --> 01:31:15,270
Put them down.

2339
01:31:15,303 --> 01:31:17,240
(children screaming)

2340
01:31:17,273 --> 01:31:19,775
Put them down, Glenn.

2341
01:31:20,810 --> 01:31:23,312
This is really getting
embarrassing, Glenn.

2342
01:31:23,345 --> 01:31:25,648
Put them down.

2343
01:31:26,415 --> 01:31:29,818
Put them down Glenn, please.

2344
01:31:29,852 --> 01:31:30,953
"I'll put 'em down."

2345
01:31:32,087 --> 01:31:36,958
And don't tilt it
either. On the tires!

2346
01:31:36,992 --> 01:31:39,028
Ow. ow.

2347
01:31:40,830 --> 01:31:42,765
OK, now pick it up again.
Come on, 10 more reps.

2348
01:31:42,798 --> 01:31:47,603
Please Glenn,
listen. Try to think.

2349
01:31:47,637 --> 01:31:50,372
You must, Glenn
please. Try to think.

2350
01:31:50,405 --> 01:31:53,008
You try to think
but nothin' happens.

2351
01:31:53,042 --> 01:31:56,578
Oh my God, I'm
Sinead O'Connor.

2352
01:31:56,612 --> 01:31:59,848
Wait here with me, Glenn.

2353
01:31:59,882 --> 01:32:01,250
They're coming for us.

2354
01:32:01,283 --> 01:32:02,552
They're coming to
take us away, ha-ha.

2355
01:32:02,585 --> 01:32:05,655
They're coming to take us
away, ho-ho, he-he, ha-ha.

2356
01:32:05,688 --> 01:32:09,392
Sis, pull my finger.

2357
01:32:09,425 --> 01:32:12,628
What am I? What am I?
Get it? Sistine Chapel.

2358
01:32:12,662 --> 01:32:17,267
Like that? I got another
one too. Watch the bunny.

2359
01:32:17,300 --> 01:32:19,135
Joyce.

2360
01:32:19,168 --> 01:32:21,737
So Glenn is pro-Joyce.

2361
01:32:25,140 --> 01:32:28,677
Aw, forget it.
Nobody loves me.

2362
01:32:28,710 --> 01:32:30,647
I gotta get some
air. It's a big country.

2363
01:32:30,680 --> 01:32:34,183
I better go see part
of it before I die.

2364
01:32:34,217 --> 01:32:36,852
Wait, Glenn, wait.

2365
01:32:38,687 --> 01:32:41,057
If you walk away now,
there's gonna be another sequel.

2366
01:32:41,090 --> 01:32:43,758
Oh, no.

2367
01:32:43,792 --> 01:32:47,297
Glenn? Glenn,
what are you doing?

2368
01:32:47,330 --> 01:32:48,330
Glenn?

2369
01:32:48,363 --> 01:32:50,900
Don't you do-
Don't do that.

2370
01:32:50,933 --> 01:32:54,203
Don't you even think
about doing that.

2371
01:32:54,237 --> 01:32:58,907
Glenn, don't.
Don't. Don't do it.

2372
01:32:58,942 --> 01:33:01,077
Don't do it Glenn.

2373
01:33:01,110 --> 01:33:03,478
Oh, stop. Glenn, no!

2374
01:33:04,580 --> 01:33:07,350
(screaming loudly)

2375
01:33:07,383 --> 01:33:10,518
He became Ted Turner
now. Colorize the movie.

2376
01:33:10,552 --> 01:33:12,288
Got shocked all
the way back to Oz.

2377
01:33:12,322 --> 01:33:15,925
Hmm-mmm. That's good voltage.

2378
01:33:17,893 --> 01:33:19,962
I don't think this method
is a final exit, guys.

2379
01:33:19,995 --> 01:33:23,765
Glenn, the Governor
called, oh nevermind.

2380
01:33:23,798 --> 01:33:26,535
He's just disappeared.
That happens.

2381
01:33:26,568 --> 01:33:28,470
- Let's us disappear.
- Okay.

2382
01:33:28,503 --> 01:33:30,072
- Shocking.
- Excuse me.

2383
01:33:33,742 --> 01:33:38,513
(doors closing hydraulically)

2384
01:33:44,187 --> 01:33:48,857
Oh boy, I gotta admit
guys, a movie that bad...

2385
01:33:48,890 --> 01:33:51,893
Yep, that was bad.
Bad City, Arizona.

2386
01:33:51,927 --> 01:33:52,895
Bad-o-rama.

2387
01:33:52,928 --> 01:33:55,832
I think it made
me kinda drowsy.

2388
01:33:55,865 --> 01:33:58,200
Bad to the b-b-bone.
Born to be bad.

2389
01:33:58,233 --> 01:33:59,502
Bad, bad, bad.

2390
01:33:59,535 --> 01:34:02,738
Born under a bad sign.
Been bad so damn long.

2391
01:34:02,772 --> 01:34:06,942
Try a piece. Taste anything?

2392
01:34:06,975 --> 01:34:09,678
I think I've tasted
something like that somewhere.

2393
01:34:09,712 --> 01:34:13,615
Tastes kinda like
Fritos, or tuna fish.

2394
01:34:13,648 --> 01:34:16,818
Yeah, I made it with my
little toe and permanent.

2395
01:34:16,852 --> 01:34:18,053
Joel, what?!

2396
01:34:18,087 --> 01:34:20,588
(spitting fiercely)

2397
01:34:20,622 --> 01:34:21,857
Give me a bite of that.

2398
01:34:21,890 --> 01:34:24,027
Yeah, Tom Servo,
you try some.

2399
01:34:25,460 --> 01:34:27,663
Hey, that one has
a tunnel of drugs.

2400
01:34:27,697 --> 01:34:29,032
Yeah, Phenobarbital.

2401
01:34:29,065 --> 01:34:30,833
Enough to knock you out
for about eight hours.

2402
01:34:30,867 --> 01:34:32,602
(yawning)

2403
01:34:32,635 --> 01:34:35,637
You guys, I'm just kidding.
We gotta read a letter.

2404
01:34:35,670 --> 01:34:37,373
It's always funny
until someone gets killed.

2405
01:34:37,407 --> 01:34:38,407
Yeah, in particularly.

2406
01:34:38,440 --> 01:34:40,375
That one hit hard. Anyway...

2407
01:34:40,408 --> 01:34:45,647
This one is a letter. Let's
put that on stillstore Cambot.

2408
01:34:45,680 --> 01:34:49,652
And it says: Greetings from
the Colorado State Prison.

2409
01:34:49,685 --> 01:34:51,720
A few of us guys
here watch your show.

2410
01:34:51,753 --> 01:34:54,490
Keeps us laughing, so please
keep up the good work.

2411
01:34:54,523 --> 01:34:56,592
Your show makes doing
time a little bit easier.

2412
01:34:56,625 --> 01:34:59,795
Your loyal fans,
Anthony, Dave, and Jack.

2413
01:34:59,828 --> 01:35:01,930
All right, that's cool.

2414
01:35:01,963 --> 01:35:03,698
Brave on.

2415
01:35:03,732 --> 01:35:05,735
Free your mind my brothers.

2416
01:35:05,768 --> 01:35:07,703
Anyway, over to you, Glenn.

2417
01:35:07,737 --> 01:35:11,340
OK. How does this work?

2418
01:35:11,373 --> 01:35:13,608
Put this up on
stillstore, Cambot,

2419
01:35:13,642 --> 01:35:17,145
or rocket number nine
I guess it would be.

2420
01:35:17,178 --> 01:35:23,052
And this one says: Dear Joel,
Tom Servo, Crow and Gypsy.

2421
01:35:23,085 --> 01:35:26,322
I like Crow because
he talks a lot.

2422
01:35:26,355 --> 01:35:27,523
I've heard it, he does.

2423
01:35:27,557 --> 01:35:30,525
No wonder he has
a big, long mouth.

2424
01:35:30,558 --> 01:35:34,930
And I like Gypsy because
she has a purple mouth.

2425
01:35:34,963 --> 01:35:37,165
But the guy I like
the most is Joel.

2426
01:35:37,198 --> 01:35:40,735
He sleeps during the
movies, who can blame him?

2427
01:35:40,770 --> 01:35:43,705
And I think Tom Servo is cute.

2428
01:35:43,738 --> 01:35:45,573
And there's a little
picture there.

2429
01:35:45,607 --> 01:35:48,410
This is from Deborah M.

2430
01:35:48,443 --> 01:35:49,612
That's a cute kid.

2431
01:35:49,645 --> 01:35:52,347
You know, I used to have
little fans like this.

2432
01:35:52,380 --> 01:35:54,650
Before my career
was cut short.

2433
01:35:54,683 --> 01:35:56,685
Hey Glenn,
thanks for the help.

2434
01:35:56,718 --> 01:35:59,555
Anytime, friend. I'll be
right here if you need me.

2435
01:35:59,588 --> 01:36:01,857
Sure thanks, and good luck.

2436
01:36:01,890 --> 01:36:04,260
Just give me a
holler. I won't be far.

2437
01:36:04,293 --> 01:36:06,695
You know, mi casa es su casa.

2438
01:36:06,728 --> 01:36:07,897
What a sweet guy.

2439
01:36:07,930 --> 01:36:09,732
Yeah. What do you think sirs?

2440
01:36:09,765 --> 01:36:14,068
Well Tom Thumb, I think
I'll be at the bakery.

2441
01:36:14,102 --> 01:36:16,738
And as for you, these
Thorazine waffles

2442
01:36:16,772 --> 01:36:20,308
should get your day off to
a heavily medicated start.

2443
01:36:20,342 --> 01:36:22,745
I had Jell-O today.

2444
01:36:22,778 --> 01:36:25,080
Just start running, Frank.

